Z||000021||reddog||12-06-2001||01:22 PM||||No.. no kill stories to speak of!! Ive just been trying to get everything working properly before I put it up against anything. Just put a new underdrive pulley and a new alternator on yesterday as well as a Harmonic balancer(Somehow it broke loose from the rubber it was pressed on and was free spinning on the shaft behind the pulley ( Old rubber meets new Hp = new balancer).I'll keep you all informed on the progress though. I still have a shift kit for my tranny that I need to have put on. Then i'll be looking for those ugly@$$ ricers with the park benches on their trunk lids. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000022||fropuff||12-06-2001||06:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>one question... why?<P><BR> a 35-37 wouldn't be really a 50... toss in a 41/20 and run 73. a 45/20 is 82, the 52 93, 62 125.4. the 41 is plenty safe. <P>these are NX only numbers. if your running NOS (05120) the numbers will be different, same with ZEX cause your not really adding fuel. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Sorry, I wan't clear.  When I said the 37 thing, I meant 37 HP; I think that's the lowest HP setting.  I should have stopped while I was ahead.  I meant to ask what jets are needed to run around a 50 shot.  I plan on doing an NX kit, so it'll be the numbers you said.  I just wanted to try the lowest first, then probably stay with the 73 HP output.  I'm probably confusing you again, so I'm done.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks for the help.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000023||reddog||12-06-2001||10:42 PM||||Travis I tried the 22 fuel jet and it backfired in second(sounded like it came from the intake). Went to 26 and it backfired in third again. Pulled hard from 2nd to 3rd but started losing power just before it backfired.Should I try the 20 fuel jet? Timing appears ok. Could the plugs be causing it? Couldn't get the NGK plugs got Autolites instead. BTW the wiring harness to the map sensor is crap/ falling apart could this be part of it. Valves need adjusting maybe. Anyone have any ideas? Any other guys out their running N2O any similar problems. first and second hit hard with no problems Why only backfiring in third?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000024||artherd||12-06-2001||11:57 PM||||You mention valves...<P>pre-ignition in the intake sounds like the intake valves might not be entirely closing?!<P>That, or I'd suspect over-heated combustion charges, but that'd be from a lean condition, and you're running rich..<P>Do you have an A/F monitor?  If not, GET ONE!<P>If you're running NO2, you need an A/F ratio monitor, peroid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I bet Travis kept his custom-installed one.<P>Backfiring under NO2 in higher gears sounds a lot like either or both of:<P>1) Just plain running so rich that you're igniting leftover fuel in the pipes.<P>2) your Ignition is NOT STRONG ENOUGH to ignite the charged mixture (this sounds like your ascendant loss of power, does this loss happen around ~3-5krpm or so? Fiero ECMs get a timing advance at 3k that will make your ignition have to work harder still)<P>Solution: MSD-6AL !<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>PS: Man you guys have two *SWEET* GTs!!<P>Reddog, I really really REALLY LOVE THOSE SEATS!  <P>Trav: even though your friend botched those 19s, the 18 and 17s look pretty killer I have to say!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000025||reddog||12-07-2001||12:28 AM||||Well I just had Travis put a msd 6a on along with the NX express kit. How do I check to make sure it is working properly? As for the valves how do I check to see if they are closing correctly and can it be that they need adjusting or would it be that the springs are worn and need to be replaced? Should I try and go with a different or colder plug? The Autolites that I have now are what the parts store had as a reference for a stock 2.8 and are gapped at 50 instead of the stock gap of 45. BTW it does not backfire at all at WOT without the spray. IT does however backfire a little on decceleration  with no spray. What causes a backfire in the intake anyway? <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||reddog||12-07-2001||12:58 AM||||OH yeah... Maybe I should mention the mods that Ive done to it so far!!!<BR>K&N filter<BR>Bored out TB and plenum from Darrel Morse<BR>New Tomco injectors<BR>Hypertech adjustable fuel pressure regulator(running @ 38 PSI at idle and 34 @ 2500rpm)<BR>Thermomaster Chip<BR>low tempurature thermostat<BR>Low temp cooling fan switch<BR>Msd 6A<BR>Accel 8.8mm plug wires <BR>Powerpulley<BR>No Cat<P>replaced :<BR>02 sensor <BR>Map sensor<BR>Mat sensor<BR>Coolant Temp sensor<BR>Aic<BR>needs replaced: <BR>has old tps <BR>Map sensor wiring harness is FUBAR<P>I took the Accel coil and ign module off and put the stock ones back on because of an intermittent miss in the ignition on the way back from Ga. It would just jerk all of the sudden and the tach would jump around really quick and then resume. Haven't really driven any real distance since replacing them so I am not sure that this fixed the problem. Also I checked the timing today and on the #1 wire it read right around the 10 mark on #4 it fluctuated at times between 11 and 10???? it still idles around 1100rpms in park and 1000rpms in gear. Does this help any?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by reddog (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
